        "Прошедшие времена, последовательность событий и короткая история с неожиданным финалом.",
        T("Language focus", "Past simple moves a story forward: I opened the door. Past continuous sets the scene or describes an action in progress: It was raining. Use when for the event that interrupts: I was walking home when I found a wallet. Use first, a few minutes later, eventually to guide your listener."),
        W("notice – заметить\nrealise – понять\nreturn – вернуть\neventually – в конце концов\nmeanwhile – тем временем\nrelieved – почувствовавший облегчение"),
        T("Read and discuss", "At eight o'clock Sam was waiting for a bus after football practice. He noticed a small bag under the seat. A phone inside was ringing. Sam answered it and spoke to the owner, who was already on another bus. Ten minutes later she came back. The bag contained her passport, and she was flying the next morning."),
        G("Use the language in context", "Sam [was waiting] for a bus when he noticed a bag.\nHe [answered] the phone and spoke to the owner.\n[Meanwhile], the owner was travelling away from the stop.\nShe felt [relieved] when Sam returned her passport.", bank=False),
        C("Read, think and choose", "Which event happened first? | The owner returned | *Sam noticed a bag | Sam went to the airport\nWhich form sets the scene? | He finds | *He was waiting | He will wait\nWhy was the bag important? | It contained football boots | *It contained a passport | It was a present"),
        L("Listen, pause and complete", "en-GB", "I was [walking] home when I heard a dog. At first I thought it was [lost], but then I saw its owner. She was looking for her [keys], and the dog was waiting beside her.", "What was the owner looking for? | Her phone | *Her keys | Her passport\nWas the dog alone? | *No, the owner was nearby | Yes, for several days | The story does not mention a dog"),
        WR("Your turn", "Write a 100–130 word story beginning 'I thought it would be an ordinary afternoon.' Set the scene with past continuous, include at least three events in past simple, and finish with a clear outcome."),
