        "lib-en-b2-media", "Beyond the headline: проверяем информацию", "en", "B2", ["Практика", "Разговорная речь"],
        "Различайте утверждение, свидетельство и вывод; тренируйте reported speech и точные формулировки.",
        T("Language focus", "A headline compresses information and may omit limitations. Ask who made the claim, what evidence supports it, and whether the evidence applies to the wider population. Reported speech can backshift tense: 'We found a link' becomes 'They said they had found a link.' A correlation alone does not establish a cause."),
        W("claim – утверждение\nevidence – свидетельства\nsample – выборка\nmisleading – вводящий в заблуждение\nsource – источник\nlimitation – ограничение"),
        T("Read and discuss", "A headline reads: 'New study proves music makes everyone more productive.' The article describes a survey of 80 volunteers who already enjoy listening to music while working. They reported feeling more focused, but researchers did not measure the quality of their work. The study may reveal a preference among these volunteers; it cannot show that music improves everyone's performance."),
        G("Use the language in context", "The researchers said they [had surveyed] eighty volunteers.\nThe headline is [misleading] because it overstates the findings.\nThe volunteers reported [feeling] more focused.\nA small self-selected [sample] may not represent everyone.", bank=False),
        C("Read, think and choose", "Which conclusion is supported? | Music improves everyone's work | *These volunteers reported feeling more focused | Music prevents all mistakes\nWhich detail is missing? | The number of participants | *An objective measure of work quality | Whether volunteers liked music\nWhich headline is most accurate? | Music guarantees success | *Music fans report better focus in a small survey | Science ends the debate"),
        L("Listen, pause and complete", "en-GB", "The editor asked whether we had checked the [source]. We had read the headline, but the original report described only a small [sample]. We changed 'proves' to 'suggests' and added the main [limitation].", "Why was the headline changed? | The report had disappeared | *It was stronger than the evidence | The editor disliked music\nWhich word replaced 'proves'? | Guarantees | *Suggests | Denies"),
        WR("Your turn", "Write a 150–180 word response to the headline in the reading. Summarise the claim, explain two limitations, and propose a more accurate headline. Distinguish what the study measured from what the headline claims."),
