        T("Read and discuss", "A team wants to release an app on Friday. The client needs a demonstration for a Monday meeting, but the developer needs two more days to test payments. They agree to demonstrate the main screens on Friday with payments disabled. The full release will follow after testing. Both sides protect the need that matters most without pretending the original plan is still possible."),
        G("Use the language in context", "If we [reduced] the scope, we could finish the demonstration by Friday.\nWould you be [willing] to move the full release to Tuesday?\nOur main [priority] is a reliable payment flow.\nThat solution sounds [feasible] within the time available.", bank=False),
        C("Read, think and choose", "What does the client actually need? | Every feature on Friday | *A demonstration before Monday's meeting | No testing\nWhat is the agreed trade-off? | Release untested payments | *Show main screens early and release payments later | Cancel the meeting\nWhich reply is constructive? | Your deadline is stupid | *I see why timing matters; could we reduce the scope? | There is nothing to discuss"),
        L("Listen, pause and complete", "en-GB", "I understand that Monday's meeting is a [priority]. If we showed the main screens on Friday, we could still test the [payments] properly. Would you be willing to treat Friday as a [demonstration] rather than a full release?", "What is proposed for Friday? | A complete release | *A demonstration | A payment deadline\nWhat remains to be tested? | The meeting room | *Payments | The client's email"),
        WR("Your turn", "Write a 150–180 word negotiation email. A client requests five new features by Friday, but only two can be tested properly. Acknowledge the deadline, offer two alternatives, explain a trade-off, and ask for a decision politely."),
