        "Меняйте тон сообщения для коллеги, клиента и официальной аудитории без потери смысла.",
        T("Language focus", "Register reflects audience, purpose and relationship. Formal writing does not require unnecessarily long words. Keep the action clear while adjusting directness: 'Send it today' can become 'Could you send the revised file by four today so we can meet the deadline?' A diplomatic refusal acknowledges the request, states the constraint, and offers a realistic alternative."),
        W("blunt – резкий, прямолинейный\ntactful – тактичный\nundertake – браться, обязаться\naccommodate – учесть пожелание\nin due course – в надлежащее время\nat short notice – в последний момент"),
        T("Read and discuss", "A client asks for a complete rewrite the evening before publication. The writer cannot undertake the work without delaying the launch. A vague reply such as 'We'll see what we can do' creates an expectation the team may not meet. A clearer response acknowledges the request, specifies which corrections are possible now, and proposes a separate date for a full rewrite."),
        G("Use the language in context", "We cannot [undertake] a complete rewrite at such short notice.\nWe can, [however], correct the factual errors before publication.\nCould you [confirm] which changes are essential by four today?\nWe would be happy to discuss the wider revision [in due course].", bank=False),
        C("Read, think and choose", "Which reply is both tactful and clear? | No. Your problem. | *We can correct the figures today; a full rewrite would require postponement | We'll probably do everything somehow\nWhat is wrong with a vague promise? | It is always too short | *It may create an unrealistic expectation | It contains no difficult vocabulary\nWhich detail helps the recipient act? | A long apology without a request | *A specific deadline and the changes to prioritise | An unrelated anecdote"),
        L("Listen, pause and complete", "en-GB", "Thank you for outlining the changes. We can [accommodate] the factual corrections today. A full rewrite would require [postponing] publication. Could you confirm whether the current launch date remains the main [priority]?", "What can be completed today? | The entire rewrite | *Factual corrections | Nothing at all\nWhat decision is requested? | Whether to hire a new team | *Whether the launch date is still the main priority | Whether to remove every paragraph"),
        WR("Your turn", "Write two versions of a reply to a last-minute rewrite request: 70–90 words to a colleague and 130–160 words to a client. Preserve the same facts, limits and proposed next step. Explain in two sentences how you adjusted register without obscuring the decision."),
